KUF port (M8): --gpu_timestamp_stats and --gpu_timestamp_sections, GPU time per guest frame

Opt-in diagnostics (default off: nothing changes). --gpu_timestamp_stats: the Vulkan command processor writes a
timestamp at the start (top of pipe) and the end (bottom of pipe) of every submitted command buffer, reads them back
after the submission's fence has signalled, sums them per guest frame (between two guest swaps, so render-only
frames count as frames), and logs every 10 s: "[gpu-time] <s> s: <n> frames, GPU ms per frame mean p50 p95 p99 max;
submissions <n>, not timed <n>". The presenter's own work (the copy to the swapchain) is not included.
--gpu_timestamp_sections (with the former): a timestamp, in the deferred command stream, at every switch between
draws, render target transfers (VulkanRenderTargetCache::PerformTransfersAndResolveClears when it has work) and
resolves (IssueCopy), and a per-frame split logged with the 10 s summary ("sections per frame: draws, transfers,
resolves"). With the GPU trace (gpu_trace_frame, patch 0009) each transfer is also logged (destination and source
render targets, EDRAM tile range, rectangles, guest pixels).
Adds vkCmdWriteTimestamp and vkGetQueryPoolResults to the device function table and a timestamp command to the
deferred command buffer.

